		</h3>
		<div id="question-138-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p data-pasted="true"><strong>Please note &ndash; The Town of Saugus has made copies of your quarterly real and personal property tax bills available through Unipay - our online payment portal. &nbsp;You do not have to pay your taxes online in order to obtain a copy of your bill.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Please contact the Assessor&apos;s office (781-231-4130) and have the mailing addresses updated or if you are not the property owner who receives directly in the mail, contact the property owners to obtain. &nbsp;If you are a 3rd party payment processor - you need to wait to obtain invoices via mail, or directly from your customers, or follow the instructions below for the self-serve option.</p><p>Real Estate, Personal Property, and Water/Sewer invoice images will be available online on our payment site on billed date - Unipay with Unibank. &nbsp;</p><p>UNIPAY Website Link: &nbsp;<a href="https://unipaygold.unibank.com/CustomerInfo.aspx">https://unipaygold.unibank.com/CustomerInfo.aspx</a> - Type &ldquo;Town of Saugus&rdquo; where indicated in the center of the page. &nbsp;There is a &ldquo;View Bills&rdquo; button at the bottom of the screen once you enter a valid account number.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
