<li id="question-139" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-139-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-139-answer">
				Parking Ticket - What are your appeal options? (PICK ONLY ONE)
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-139-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p data-pasted="true">The Treasurer&apos;s Office takes payments for parking tickets and/or can assist you with your appeal options. No one in the Treasurer&apos;s Office can reduce or negate your ticket, we can only guide you towards an appeal option.</p><h2 class="subhead1"><strong>TWO OPTIONS FOR PARKING TICKET APPEALS AS SHOWN BELOW</strong></h2><p><strong>IN WRITING - MAIL PAYMENTS &amp; APPEALS TO: &nbsp;Town of Saugus - 298 Central Street, Suite 5, Saugus, MA &nbsp;01906 -&nbsp;</strong>You can make a handwritten appeal. &nbsp;The ticket will be placed on hold until the next review/hearing date &ndash; and you will be notified by mail and/or email with the Hearing Officer&rsquo;s resolution. &nbsp;Your appeal must be received within 21 days of the ticket date. &nbsp;You can mail your appeal letter with a copy of your ticket &ndash; and a copy of your HP placard (if applicable) to Town of Saugus, Parking Hearings Officer, 298 Central Street, Suite 5, Saugus, MA &nbsp;01906. &nbsp;Forms are available at the Treasurer&rsquo;s Office or <a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1497" target="_blank" rel="noopener">see document link</a> - if you wish to fill out a written appeal immediately.</p><p><strong>ONLINE - ONLINE PAYMENTS &amp; APPEALS CAN BE DONE AT:</strong> You can <a href="https://saugusma.rmcpay.com/">make an online appeal&nbsp;</a>&ndash; using the web address on the ticket -<a data-fr-linked="true" href="https://saugusma.rmcpay.com/"></a> click &quot;Appeal&quot;. &nbsp;You can upload pictures and/or a detailed letter to go with your appeal. &nbsp;The ticket will be placed on hold until the next review/hearing date &ndash; and you will be notified by email with the Hearing Officer&rsquo;s resolution. *NOTE - If you make an appeal online - you will also receive a MAILED response. &nbsp;</p><p>If you enter the appeal online, and then send in writing - the appeal received FIRST will be taken. &nbsp;It will not be reviewed again.</p><p>If you are not satisfied with your appeal result, you must request a Judicial Court Review at the Essex Superior Court to further appeal. &nbsp;A filing fee will apply to submit a Judicial Court Review. &nbsp;You will have to call the courthouse to inquire as to the cost. &nbsp;Once the Town of Saugus Hearings Officer has made his decision, he will not review again.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-107" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-107-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-107-answer">
				I am selling my property, how do I obtain a final Water and Sewer Bill?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-107-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Contact the Utility Billing Department of the Collector / Treasurer&apos;s Office at 781-231-4139 <strong>two weeks prior</strong> to the closing to have the final water reading scheduled.&nbsp;</p><p>Final water readings are prepared on Thursdays. &nbsp;</p><p>Final water reading invoices will be prepared after the reading is obtained from your UltraSonic SMART meter. &nbsp;If the new UltraSonic SMART meter has not been installed when scheduling the final water reading, you will be required to do so before the final reading can be completed. &nbsp;The Utility Billing Manager will coordinate an appointment with the installation company (Mass Installation Inc.) and a representative of the seller to have the UltraSonic SMART meter installed. &nbsp;Once installed, the final reading will be prepared and emailed to the seller&apos;s representative at the email provided to receive the final reading. &nbsp;The final reading invoice can be paid at the Town Hall Collector/Treasurer&apos;s Office or mailed to the same, or submitted to your attorney for payment to be distributed from the closing.</p><p>The mailing address is: &nbsp;Collector/Treasurer&apos;s Office, 298 Central Street, Suite 5, Saugus, MA&nbsp; 01906.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-108" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-108-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-108-answer">
				I bought the property this year, why is the former owner still appearing on the Real Estate Tax bill?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-108-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Property taxes are billed with the information as of January 1st preceding the beginning of the current Fiscal Year. If you purchased the property any time after January 1st, you are not listed as the assessed owner until the next fiscal year. This rule is mandated by Massachusetts General Law. The town's Fiscal year runs from July 1st to June 30th each year. If the Assessors Office is notified that there is a new owner, as a courtesy the Assessors can add your name in "Care Of".</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-109" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-109-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-109-answer">
				What types of Special Assessments can be added to my Real Estate Tax bill?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-109-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>There are three Special Assessments that are currently being billed to property owners on their Real Estate tax bill. Apportioned Sewer Assessment, Apportioned Septic Assessment, and Unpaid and Overdue Water and Sewer charges. The Apportioned Sewer Assessment is a 10-year fee paid for the installation of sewer pipeline in front of your property, the Apportioned Septic Assessment is also a 10-year fee for loans granted to improve septic systems that have failed Title V, and Unpaid and Overdue Water and Sewer charges are the charges billed to property owners for Water and Sewer service on a bi-annual basis. In order to avoid these Special Assessments be sure pay these charges as they are originally billed.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-110" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-110-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-110-answer">
				When does interest accrue on unpaid bills?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-110-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>If you are unable to pay your tax bill, Massachusetts General Law mandates that interest at 14% be added to the amount due from the due date to the date of payment. A tax bill is considered &quot;paid&quot; upon receipt by the Treasurer / Collector not the post mark on the envelope.</p><p>The Fiscal Years taxes must be paid in full by the May 1st due date to avoid any further action to collect. Other collection fees can apply.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-111" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-111-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-111-answer">
				What if I can&#x2019;t pay my Real Estate Tax bill?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-111-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>First check with the Town of Saugus Assessor's Office to see if you qualify for a tax exemption or tax deferral. If you still owe taxes, please contact the Town Collector as soon as possible. Although we cannot eliminate the tax, we can listen to your situation and offer possible solutions.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-112" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-112-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-112-answer">
				What is a municipal lien certificate and how much does it cost?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-112-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>A Municipal Lien Certificate is a certificate prepared by the Town of Saugus which lists any and all taxes and charges which may be due on a parcel. If you wish to request a Municipal Lien Certificate you need to do so in writing by providing us with the address and any other identifying information such as Owner and Map Block and Lot. Please be sure to include a self-addressed stamped envelope and the appropriate fee as shown here. Once we receive the request, a certificate will be prepared within ten business days.</p><ul><li>$50 Residential Single Family to Three Family</li><li>$100 Residential of Four Family or more</li><li>$50 Farms, forest land and all other real property</li><li>$150 Commercial, industrial, or public utility structure</li></ul></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-113" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-113-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-113-answer">
				How can I pay my bills?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-113-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>All taxes can be paid by cash, personal check, or money order by mail or in person at the Town Hall. Online payments are accepted thru this website - click on Online Payments and you will be linked to the Unipay online payment portal with Unibank.</p><p>If you are unable to make payment during regular business hours, a white payment box is available in front of Town Hall. <strong>Do not</strong> make payments in cash - use this for checks <strong>only</strong>.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-114" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-114-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-114-answer">
				When does interest accrue on unpaid bills?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-114-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Excise tax is due and payable 30 days from the date of issue. If you are unable to pay your tax bill, Massachusetts General Law mandates that interest at 12% be added to the amount due from the due date to the date of payment. A tax bill is considered &quot;paid&quot; upon receipt by the Treasurer / Collector, not the post mark on the envelope. Other collection fees can be added.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-141" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-141-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-141-answer">
				FAQs - Motor Vehicle Excise Tax
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-141-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p data-pasted="true">For a guide from the Secretary of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts with regards to penalty and interest calculations; abatements; excise calculations; etc see the <a href="https://www.mass.gov/guides/motor-vehicle-excise">Commonwealth of Massachusetts Motor Vehicle Excise page</a>.</p><p>To contact the <a data-fr-linked="true" href="//Mass.gov">Mass.gov</a> Customer Service, Excise Division - please call 1-857-368-8180. &nbsp;</p><p><strong>What valuation is used for motor vehicle excise bills? </strong>&nbsp;The excise is based on the value of the motor vehicle as determined by the Commissioner of Revenue upon certain percentages of the manufacturer&apos;s list price in the year of manufacture. The excise valuation is not based on the actual purchase price or &quot;book value&quot; of the vehicle. The percentages set forth in the statutory depreciation schedule that are applied to manufacturer&apos;s list price are as follows:</p><p>In the year preceding the designated year of manufacture 50%</p><p>In the year of manufacture 90%</p><p>In the second year 60%</p><p>In the third year 40%</p><p>In the fourth year 25%</p><p>In the fifth and succeeding years 10%</p><p><strong>What is the rate of excise and where is it assessed? &nbsp;</strong>An excise in the amount of $25 per thousand is assessed upon the value of the vehicle as determined in accordance with the depreciation schedule. Prior to 1981 the rate was $66 per thousand. With the passage of Proposition 2 1/2 the rate was set at $25 per thousand. The excise is levied for a full calendar year and is assessed by the community where the motor vehicle is customarily garaged. In those instances where vehicles are registered in the Commonwealth but garaged outside of Massachusetts, the Commissioner of Revenue assesses the excise which is paid into the State treasury. M.G.L. Ch. 60A Sec. 1 provides that the owner of any motor vehicle registered for less than a full calendar year will be obligated to pay an excise based on the entire month when the vehicle was registered, as well as the remaining months of the year. For example, a vehicle registered on April 9th will be assessed an excise for the months of April through December.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-115" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-115-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-115-answer">
				What happens if I do not pay my Motor Vehicle Excise Tax?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-115-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>If your Motor Vehicle Excise Tax bill is not satisfied, either through making payment or receiving an abatement, you will receive a "Demand" notice which includes interest at the rate of 12% per annum and $5 demand fee which is due within fourteen days from the date of issue. If this tax remains unsatisfied the bill will be referred to the town's Deputy Tax Collector for further collection activity which includes being issued and served with a "Warrant to Collect" and your Excise Tax being "Marked" at the Massachusetts Registry of Motor Vehicles for non-renewal of your Driver's License and Vehicle or Trailer registration.</p><p>It should be noted that several other states have mutual agreements with the Commonwealth of Massachusetts to detain or impound "Marked" vehicles found in other states where there is an outstanding Excise Tax.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-117" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-117-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-117-answer">
				What do I do if I receive a Motor Vehicle Excise Tax bill from Saugus, but I am no longer living in the Town of Saugus?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-117-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Under certain circumstances you may still be required to pay the Excise Tax to the Town of Saugus. If you do not live in the Town of Saugus when you receive the bill, but you did live in the Town of Saugus either on January 1st of the tax year, or when you registered the vehicle or trailer, you should still pay the Excise Tax to the Town of Saugus. You should then contact the Massachusetts Registry of Motor Vehicles to <strong>change</strong> both your mailing address and the city or town in which your vehicle is <strong>principally garaged</strong> (known as the garage code). Both of these items need to be changed with the Mass. RMV in order for you to receive your next Excise Tax bill from your new community rather than the Town of Saugus. There is a link to the Massachusetts Registry of Motor Vehicles on the first page of the Collector / Treasurers Office.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-116" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-116-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-116-answer">
				How do I pay overdue Motor Vehicle Excise Taxes that have been marked at the Registry of Motor Vehicles for non-renewal?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-116-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Please contact our Deputy Collector, PKS Associates at 781-944-8504. You must make payment directly to their office. Once they receive payment from you, they will contact the Registry of Motor Vehicles to release your account so that you can renew your license and / or registration.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-118" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-118-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-118-answer">
				I received a Motor Vehicle Excise Tax bill on a car I no longer own. Where do I go for an adjustment?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-118-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Please contact the Town of Saugus Assessor's Office for abatement information.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-119" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-119-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-119-answer">
				What do I do if I feel my Motor Vehicle Excise amount is incorrect?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-119-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>You may file for an abatement of your tax with the Board of Assessors. If you contact the Board of Assessors at 781-231-4130, the Assessors&apos; Staff will be able to assist you with any questions you may have relative to completing the appropriate forms to file for an abatement.</p><p>Please remember that filing for an abatement of your tax does not stay any collection activity. You should pay your Excise Tax as you were billed and if you are granted an abatement from the Assessors, you will receive a credit to your tax bill and, if applicable, a refund.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-120" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-120-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-120-answer">
				How often should I expect to receive a Motor Vehicle Excise Tax bill from the Town?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-120-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>You should expect to receive one Excise Tax bill relative to each calendar year during which the vehicle is registered. If the vehicle was not registered for an entire year, then the Excise Tax will be pro-rated according to the number of months during which the vehicle was registered - from the date of registration. It should be noted that under Massachusetts General Law, proration of the Excise Tax is only allowed on a per month basis.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-121" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-121-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-121-answer">
				When does interest accrue on unpaid bills?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-121-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Water and Sewer charges are due and payable 30 days from the date of issue. Interest at the rate of 14% per annum begins to accrue from the due date to the date of payment. A Water and Sewer bill is considered &quot;paid&quot; upon receipt by the Treasurer/Collector, not the post mark on the envelope. Late fees of $5 for unpaid water and $5 for unpaid sewer fees are also added once the &quot;Demand&quot; notice is sent.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-142" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-142-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-142-answer">
				Questions on your Water and Sewer Utility bill?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-142-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Problem with your invoice? &nbsp;Or questions about your invoice? &nbsp;</p><p>Please call the Treasurer/Collector&apos;s Office, Utility Billing at 781-231-4139 and 781-231-4135 or email <a data-fr-linked="true" href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#6c010918091e18090f042c1f0d190b191f41010d420b031a" data-pasted="true"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="325f574657404657515a724153475547411f5f531c555d44">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> or<a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#5b2f293e3a282e293e291b283a2e3c2e2876363a753c342d">&nbsp;<span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="2e5a5c4b4f5d5b5c4b5c6e5d4f5b495b5d03434f00494158">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-122" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-122-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-122-answer">
				What happens if I do not pay my Water and Sewer bill?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-122-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>In addition to the assessment of a late charge, Water and Sewer bills that are issued in the prior Fiscal Year and remain outstanding when the first actual tax bill is issued January 1st will be added to the Real Estate Tax on the property. These amounts will then be collected in the same manner as Real Estate Taxes which includes the assessment of interest and the possibility of a lien being recorded against the property.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-143" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-143-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-143-answer">
				Is Your Water Bill Higher than Normal?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-143-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Is your water bill higher than normal? You could have a leak!</p><ul><li>The meter doesn&apos;t run unless water runs through it</li><li>If a meter is starting to fail, it will slow down, not speed up</li><li>Water issues flowing through your meter are your responsibility. &nbsp;Please contact your plumber to give you house a check up</li><li>Outside sprinkler systems can have sprinkler heads that crack during winter months and can cause excessive water usage, and remember - that green lawn during this summer&apos;s drought will cause a great increase in your invoice.</li><li>Less frequently used toilets can develop leaks in the tank and cause the toilet to run/refill when not in use. &nbsp;You will have to replace the kit inside the tank.</li><li>Visit the MWRA Conservation page for more tips: &nbsp;<a data-fr-linked="true" href="http://www.mwra.com/comsupport/waterconservationmain.htm">http://www.mwra.com/comsupport/waterconservationmain.htm</a></li><li>Do you have a bathroom or toilet you don&apos;t use as much? &nbsp;You could have developed a leak. Water saver/testing products are available free of charge at the Treasurer&apos;s Office.</li><li>Check for water flow through your meter - Stop running all faucets and appliances that use water, and then go to your basement, locate your meter, flip the top cover and watch the small white triangle in the middle. &nbsp;If water is not being used, the triangle will not move. &nbsp;If it is moving, the water is being called for somewhere in your residence. &nbsp;You will need to call your plumber to help you locate the leak.</li><li>Check your current usage, by reading the meter in your basement (flip top of meter up and record all of the digits shown), then call 781.231.4139 with the reading. &nbsp;The Water Billing Department can counsel you, on how much you have used since the last reading done in August.</li></ul></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-123" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-123-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-123-answer">
				What is the Water Discount Program and do I qualify?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-123-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>The Water Discount Program is a 10% discount offered once a year to residents of the Town of Saugus who meet the following conditions:</p><ul><li>The applicant must receive a real estate tax exemption from the Board of Assessors.</li><li>The applicant must be the owner of record of the property for which the discount is requested and his/her name must appear on the water and sewer bill for that property.</li><li>The consumption of water, by the applicant, shall not exceed 3,000 cu ft for the two prior consecutive water bills issued.</li><li>The discount shall only apply to owner occupied single-family homes.</li><li>This discount will be applied on water and sewer bills issued in the spring of each year.</li></ul><p>An application for the 10% water discount must be submitted each year during the period of January 1st to March 31st. The amount of the discount is figured on 10% of the minimum water charge in effect at the time of the application.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-124" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-124-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-124-answer">
				I received a Parking Violation, how can I pay it?
			</button>
		</h3>
		<div id="question-124-answer" class="accordion-collapse collapse show">
			<div class="accordion-body">
				<div class="accordion-text redesign-text fr-view"><p>Parking Violations can be paid by cash, personal check, or money order by mail or in person at the Town Hall. If the parking ticket has been &quot;Marked&quot; at the Registry of Motor Vehicles for non-renewal on your license or registration, you must make payment in the form of cash or money order. Personal checks will not be accepted.<br><br>If you are unable to make payment during regular business hours, a yellow payment box is available in front of Town Hall. <strong>Do not</strong> make payments in cash - use this for checks <strong>only</strong>.</p></div>
				<span class="badge text-body category-pill rounded-pill mw-100 text-truncate">Treasurer / Collector</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</li>
                


<li id="question-125" class="list-group-item accordion px-0 pt-3 faq-question-item edit-container"
	data-subcategory-id="">
	<div class="position-relative accordion-item shadow-sm">
		<h3 class="accordion-header faq-question-header">
			<button class="accordion-button gap-3 z-0" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
				data-bs-target="#question-125-answer" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="question-125-answer">
